  "Origin": "起源",
  "In 2018 I was watching an earthquake livestream and asked another person in the chat, someone who was also recording earthquakes, whether we could keep talking on Discord. That question became TWERG.": "2018 年，我在看地震直播时，问了聊天室里另一位同样在记录地震的人，能不能到 Discord 继续聊。昔日问题，后来变成了 TWERG。",
  "It grew into the earliest long-running earth science community on Discord in the Chinese-speaking world: earthquakes, typhoons, heavy rain and everything in between, shared as fast and as accurately as we can.": "它成长为中文圈最早、以 Discord 为主的长期地球科学社区：地震、台风、暴雨，以及其间的一切，我们都尽可能又快又准地分享出去。",
  "Timeline": "时间轴",
  "TWERG is founded": "TWERG 成立",
  "A Discord server for people who record earthquakes.": "一个给记录地震的人的 Discord 服务器。",
  "Beyond Taiwan": "走进国际",
  "Japan Meteorological Agency data joins the feed; the first community seismology exam is held.": "接入日本气象厅数据；举办第一次社区地震考试。",
  "A full earth science platform": "完整的地球科学平台",
  "Earthquakes are joined by weather, typhoons and the rest of earth science; the entry exam is retired so anyone can join.": "除了地震，也加入天气、台风与其他地球科学；取消入群考试，让任何人都能加入。",
  "Website v3 and DYFI": "网站 v3 与 DYFI",
  "A rebuilt twerg.org launches with a scientific felt-report system.": "重新打造的 twerg.org 上线，并推出具科学依据的体感回报系统。",
  "The largest earth science community on Discord in the Chinese-speaking world.": "中文圈震级最大的 Discord 地球科学社区。",
  "What I built": "我做的东西",
  "Five things,": "五件作品，",
  "built by hand.": "亲手打造。",
  "The twerg.org home page": "twerg.org 首页",
  "01 / Website": "01 / 网站",
  "The community's home: live earthquake reports, a notable-earthquake archive, a changelog and policies. Built by me, in four languages.": "社区内核：实时地震报告、显著地震数据库、更新日志与使用规范。由我打造，支持四种语言。",
  "A felt-intensity map of Taiwan built from public reports": "由民众回报绘制的台湾体感烈度地图",
  "02 / DYFI": "02 / DYFI",
  "Did You Feel It?": "您感受到了吗？",
  "A felt-report system that turns what people feel into a town-level intensity map, checked against instruments. More on it below.": "把人们的感受转换成乡镇级烈度地图的体感回报系统，并与仪器数据交叉比对。下面有更多说明。",
  "A heavy rain advisory map of Taiwan": "台湾暴雨特报地图",
  "03 / Heavy rain": "03 / 暴雨",
  "Rain advisory map": "暴雨特报地图",
  "Official heavy rain advisories redrawn as a clean town-level map, paired with a second map for work and school closures.": "把官方的暴雨特报重新绘制成清楚的乡镇级地图，并搭配另一张停班停课地图。",
  "A typhoon warning map with forecast track and wind radii": "包含预测路径与暴风半径的台风警报图",
  "04 / Typhoon": "04 / 台风",
  "Typhoon track map": "台风路径图",
  "Forecast track, potential path, storm radii and warning areas in one frame, built to be shared as soon as a warning is issued.": "预测路径、潜势范围、暴风半径与警戒区域收进同一张图，警报一发布就能立刻分享。",
  "05 / System": "05 / 系统",
  "Readable by everyone": "每个人都看得懂",
  "Hazard colors follow a color-universal design palette so they stay distinguishable for color-blind readers, with no decorative gradients or glow.": "灾害配色采用色彩通用设计，让色觉辨识不同的读者也能分辨；不用装饰性的渐层与光晕。",
  "Deep dive": "深入",
  "DYFI,": "体感回报，",
  "done properly.": "深入研究成果。",
  "A shaking map built from people instead of sensors. Getting it right meant reading the research, and then finding where a naive version goes wrong.": "一张由人而不是传感器画出来的烈度地图。要做对，得先读懂研究，再找出直觉做法错在哪里。",
  "How a felt report becomes a map": "一笔体感回报如何变成地图",
  "Reports": "回报",
  "Consensus": "共识",
  "Intensity": "烈度",
  "Check": "验证",
  "Map": "地图",
  "01 / Foundation": "01 / 基础",
  "Built on USGS \"Did You Feel It?\"": "以 USGS「Did You Feel It?」为基础",
  "The method follows the USGS framework for community decimal intensity, then maps the result onto the Central Weather Administration's own intensity scale so it speaks the same language as official reports.": "方法沿用 USGS 的社区十进位烈度（CDI）框架，再把结果对应到中央气象署的烈度分级，让它和官方报告说同一种语言。",
  "02 / The mistake I fixed": "02 / 我修正的错误",
  "Never average people.": "别把人平均。",
  "The obvious approach, scoring each person and averaging the scores, quietly breaks: someone who was outdoors cannot answer the indoor questions, and a naive average drags the whole area down. Following Quitoriano and Wald, the system first finds the community's consensus on each question, then computes one intensity for the area.": "直觉的做法是替每个人算分再取平均，但它会悄悄出错：人在户外的人无法回答室内的题目，直接平均会把整个地区的烈度拉低。依照 Quitoriano 与 Wald 的做法，系统先找出社区对每一题的共识，再为整个地区算出一个烈度。",
  "03 / The questions": "03 / 问卷",
  "Three kinds of evidence": "三种证据",
  "What people felt, what moved indoors and what happened outside are weighed as separate factors, with an anchor question that grounds the rest.": "人的感受、室内物品的晃动、户外发生的事，分成三个因子各自衡量，并有一道锚定题作为基准。",
  "04 / Place": "04 / 地点",
  "Town by town": "一个乡镇一个乡镇",
  "Reports are located to their town, grouped on a grid and cleaned of outliers. \"I didn't feel it\" is kept too, because it marks where the shaking stopped.": "回报会定位到所在的乡镇、以网格聚合，并过滤离群值。「我没有感觉」也会保留，因为它标出了摇晃停止的地方。",
  "05 / Trust": "05 / 可信度",
  "Checked against instruments": "与仪器比对",
  "Every area is compared with nearby seismic stations and with an intensity prediction model, so reports that do not fit the physics are flagged.": "每个地区都会和附近的地震测站、以及烈度预测模型比对，不符合物理规律的回报会被标记出来。",
  "06 / Privacy": "06 / 隐私",
  "Nothing personal kept": "不留下个人数据",
  "Abuse protection stores only a one-way hash of an address, deleted automatically within about two days.": "防滥用机制只保存地址的单向哈希值，大约两天内会自动删除。",
  "References: Wald et al. 2012, Annals of Geophysics / Quitoriano & Wald 2020, Frontiers in Earth Science / Gupta 2014, Stanford University / CWA seismic intensity scale, 2020": "参考文献：Wald et al. 2012, Annals of Geophysics / Quitoriano & Wald 2020, Frontiers in Earth Science / Gupta 2014, Stanford University / 中央气象署地震烈度分级，2020",
