  "Estimating earthquake shaking when the rupture has a direction.": "当地震的破裂有方向时，如何估计摇晃的程度。",
  "The problem": "问题",
  "A point": "一个点，",
  "is not a fault.": "不是一条断层。",
  "Early warning systems usually treat an earthquake as a single point, so predicted shaking fades the same way in every direction. That works for small events.": "地震预警系统通常把地震当成一个点，因此预估的摇晃会往每个方向以相同的速度衰减。对小地震来说，这样没问题。",
  "Large, shallow earthquakes are different. The rupture <strong>travels</strong> along the fault, and it throws stronger shaking ahead of itself. Places in that direction can feel far more than a point-source estimate says. In early warning, that is the worst kind of error: <strong>telling people it is weaker than it is.</strong>": "大型的浅层地震不一样。破裂会沿着断层<strong>移动</strong>，并把更强的摇晃推向前方。位在那个方向的地方，感受到的可能远比点源估计大得多。在地震预警里，这是最糟的一种错误：<strong>告诉大家摇得比实际还轻。</strong>",
  "The method": "方法",
  "01 / Listen": "01 / 倾听",
  "Watch the shaking fade": "看摇晃怎么衰减",
  "As stations report in, compare how quickly peak ground acceleration drops off toward the east, south, west and north.": "随着测站陆续回传数据，比较最大地动加速度（PGA）往东、南、西、北衰减的速度。",
  "02 / Infer": "02 / 推论",
  "Find the direction": "找出方向",
  "If shaking fades unevenly, the rupture is moving. The imbalance points the way it is travelling.": "如果各方向的衰减不一致，代表破裂正在移动；这个不平衡，就指向它前进的方向。",
  "03 / Correct": "03 / 修正",
  "Raise what lies ahead": "调高前方的烈度",
  "Areas in front of the rupture get their estimated intensity raised. Areas behind it are left alone.": "破裂前方地区的预估烈度会被调高，后方的地区则维持不变。",
  "04 / Update": "04 / 更新",
  "Keep listening": "持续倾听",
  "The estimate is not a one-time calculation. It moves up and down every second as new data arrives, and is only pushed to people once it makes sense.": "这个估计不是一次算完就结束。它会随着新数据每秒上下调整，等结果合理了才推送给大家。",
  "Directivity correction informed by Jan et al. (2018). Station data from the P-Alert network.": "方向性修正参考 Jan et al.（2018）。测站数据来自 P-Alert 观测网。",
  "Replay / Retrospective simulation": "重播 / 回溯模拟",
  "Watch it": "看它",
  "correct itself.": "自己修正。",
